course: dictionary
lesson: 10108
title: Third: order, parts and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word third can mean three different things, and the words around it show which one. «The third time» means number 3 in order, after first and second. Third place in a race wins a bronze medal.
explain: A third is also a part of a whole: one of three equal parts, written 1/3. «Most grown-ups spend about a third of their weekdays at work» means their working days are split into three equal parts, and work takes up one of them.
explain: Ask yourself what the word is describing. A place in a line, like «the third floor», is about order. A share of something, like «a third of the class», is about parts. If you can swap in «number 3 in order» and it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Third means number 3 in order, after first and second.
fact: A third is one of three equal parts of a whole, written 1/3.
fact: To find one third of a total, divide it by 3: one third of 12 is 4.
fact: Two thirds is the rest, the two parts that are left after one third.
fact: «Third time lucky» is a saying that means something may work on the third try.
exercise: «Most grown-ups spend about a third of their weekdays at work.» What does a third mean here? | *One of three equal parts of the week | Third place in a race | The third day of the week | Third gear in a car
exercise: «A third of 12 is 4.» How do you find one third of 12? | Multiply 12 by 3 | *Divide 12 by 3 | Take 3 away from 12 | Add 3 to 12
exercise: Ella lives on the third floor. What does third mean? | *Number 3 in order, after first and second | A bronze medal | One of three equal parts | A small car
test: In «third time lucky», what does third mean? | The last one of all | Half of a set | Three minutes | *The third try
test: «Asia is the largest continent, almost a third of all land.» What does almost a third mean? | Exactly half | *Close to one of three equal parts | Nearly all | Less than one tenth
exam: Maya runs a race and finishes third. What does third mean here? | Second place, which wins a silver medal | *Third place, which wins a bronze medal | Last in the race | First place, which wins gold
